newReturnKindT -- SEQ 527 R2 (2026-11-04): what a compiled function hands back when it is not a count, on both roads, against the plain run (pop.sh inserts
jitter; before the first call). s a string literal, m a local string, d a number literal, c a computed number, l a local number, k / v counts (the controls; a
non-zero count must stay a count), h a holder, f no return at all (new road: nothing, A3; old road: the last statement's value), e a return in an arm.
